1.5 Middleware order in app.js

requestId → helmet → cors({origin: allow-list, credentials:true}) → morgan → global rateLimit (100/min) → express.json({limit:'1mb'}) → cookieParser → sanitize → routes under /api/v1 → static /uploads → 404 handler → errorHandler. Stricter rate limits on /auth/* (10/min), /public/* (20/min), /ai/* (10/min).

1.6 Auth (spec sections 13.4 and 16)
POST /auth/login: verify bcrypt hash; issue access JWT (sub, orgId, role, zoneIds, tokenVersion), 15 min, returned in JSON body; issue refresh token (random 64 bytes) stored hashed in sessions with familyId, sent as httpOnly, sameSite:'strict', secure in production cookie.
POST /auth/refresh: rotate refresh token; if a revoked token is reused, revoke the whole family and return 401.
POST /auth/logout: revoke session, clear cookie.
GET /auth/me: return user, zones, and the permission map for the role so the frontend never duplicates the matrix.
authenticate middleware: verify JWT, load user (cache 60 s in memory), reject if status !== 'active' or tokenVersion mismatch.
Public citizen self-registration: POST /auth/register-citizen creates role citizen only.
Deactivating a user or changing a role increments tokenVersion and revokes sessions.
1.7 RBAC (spec section 9), implement exactly

common/permissions.js exports ROLE_PERMS for roles admin, supervisor, engineer, auditor, citizen, mapping each permission (asset:read, asset:create, asset:update, asset:status:operate, asset:status:retire, workorder:assign, audit:read, and the full catalogue from spec 9.3) to a scope: 'org' | 'zone' | 'own' | 'public'. Fill it from the matrix in spec 9.4.

js
// middleware/authorize.js
export const authorize = (perm) => (req, res, next) => {
  const scope = ROLE_PERMS[req.user.role]?.[perm];
  if (!scope) return deny(req, res, perm);           // 403 + audit(outcome:'denied')
  req.scope = buildScopeFilter(scope, req.user);     // {orgId} | {orgId, zoneId:{$in}} | {orgId, createdBy|assigneeId}
  next();
};

Rules that must be implemented in services:

Merge req.scope into every list and single-record query. Out-of-scope single reads return 404, not 403.
Engineer PATCH /assets/:id may change only name, address, specs, notes, location (within 25 m); reject other fields with 403.
Only Admin can move an asset to decommissioned or disposed, and a reason is required.
Engineer can only do installed → in_service on assets they created.
Supervisor cannot change zoneId; only Admin can.
Work order complete: assignee, or Supervisor or Admin in scope.
Cannot demote or deactivate the last active Admin; users cannot change their own role (409/403).
Citizen sees only /public/* and their own reports; GET /public/assets/:assetCode returns only assetCode, name, category, status.
Every denied action is written to auditLogs.
1.8 Models and indexes

