1.9 Business logic
assets/lifecycle.js: state machine and role rules from spec 16.1; invalid transition returns 409; each transition writes assetEvents + auditLogs inside withTransaction.
assets/health.js: health score formula and risk levels from spec 16.2; store health.factors; recompute on inspection create, work order change, and nightly.
Inspection create: insert inspection, update asset.lastInspection, nextInspectionDue = inspectedAt + category.inspectionIntervalDays, recompute health, write event, all in one transaction.
Work order: create, assign (assignee must belong to the asset's zone), start (asset → under_maintenance), complete (transaction: update order, append log, recompute health, restore in_service when no other open orders, write event), cancel with reason, comments capped at 50.
Citizen report: create with trackingCode, $near match within 50 m on active assets, auto-create work order (source:'citizen_report'), status updates.
Asset specs validated against category.specSchema (required, type, number bounds).
Media: Multer saves to UPLOAD_DIR (jpeg/png/webp, max 5 MB), save metadata in media, return URL. Structure the code behind a storage adapter so Cloudinary or S3 can be swapped in later.
AI: modules/ai with DamageDetector interface. Implement MockDetector (deterministic pseudo-result from file size and hash) and a HostedVisionDetector that is used only if VISION_API_KEY is set; 8 s timeout; on failure return {status:'unavailable'}.
Dashboard: $facet aggregation from spec 12.5, scope-aware; cost trend by month.
Jobs (node-cron): nightly health recompute, daily preventive work order generation (idempotent), daily overdue notifications.
